rge-sound"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/king-george-sound.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King George Sound</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">King George Sound is a large natural harbour on the south coast of Western Australia, on which the town of Albany stands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-hancock"><span class="enc-name">King Hancock</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Hancock was a Tuscarora leader in North Carolina, chief of the southern Tuscarora towns around Catechna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-helu-of-wu"><span class="enc-name">King Helü of Wu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Helü was king of Wu from 514 to 496 BCE, after seizing the throne by having his cousin King Liao assassinated.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-huai-of-chu"><span class="enc-name">King Huai of Chu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Huai of Chu ruled the state of Chu from 328 to 299 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-huan-of-zhou"><span class="enc-name">King Huan of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Huan of Zhou reigned from 719 to 697 BCE as the second king of the Eastern Zhou.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-hui-of-chu"><span class="enc-name">King Hui of Chu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Hui of Chu (reigned 488–432 BCE) was a ruler of the State of Chu who restored its power after the Wu invasion of 506 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-huiwen-of-qin"><span class="enc-name">King Huiwen of Qin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Huiwen of Qin ruled the State of Qin from 338 to 311 BCE.</